{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011QRW8aejNXjUqQvvPWd7d4","type":"tool_result","content":"                                          alustosa@alustosa-thinkpadp1gen7\n               .',;::::;,'.               ────────────────────────────────\n           .';:cccccccccccc:;,.             OS  Fedora Linux 44 (Workstation Edition) x86_64\n        .;cccccccccccccccccccccc;.          Kernel  Linux 7.1.8-200.fc44.x86_64\n      .:cccccccccccccccccccccccccc:.       󰅐 Uptime  8 days, 19 hours, 51 mins\n    .;ccccccccccccc;.:dddl:.;ccccccc;.      Shell  bash 5.3.9\n   .:ccccccccccccc;OWMKOOXMWd;ccccccc:.     Terminal  claude\n  .:ccccccccccccc;KMMc;cc;xMMc;ccccccc:.  ────────────────────────────────\n  ,cccccccccccccc;MMM.;cc;;WW:;cccccccc,   󰻠 CPU  Intel(R) Core(TM) Ultra 7 165H (12+8+2) @ 5.00 GHz\n  :cccccccccccccc;MMM.;cccccccccccccccc:   󰍛 GPU  Intel Arc Graphics @ 2.30 GHz [Integrated]\n  :ccccccc;oxOOOo;MMM000k.;cccccccccccc:    RAM  50.73 GiB / 62.23 GiB (82%)\n  cccccc;0MMKxdd:;MMMkddc.;cccccccccccc;   󰋊 Disk  247.24 GiB / 952.27 GiB (26%) - btrfs\n  ccccc;XMO';cccc;MMM.;cccccccccccccccc'  ────────────────────────────────\n  ccccc;MMo;ccccc;MMW.;ccccccccccccccc;    󰍹 Display  1920x1200 in 16\", 60 Hz [Built-in]\n  ccccc;0MNc.ccc.xMMd;ccccccccccccccc;     󰍹 Display  1920x1080 in 24\", 144 Hz [External]\n  cccccc;dNMWXXXWM0:;cccccccccccccc:,      󰍹 Display  3440x1440 in 34\", 100 Hz [External]\n  cccccccc;.:odl:.;cccccccccccccc:,.        DE  KDE Plasma 6.7.4\n  ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc:'.          WM  KWin\n  :ccccccccccccccccccccccc:;,..           \n   ':cccccccccccccccc::;,.                  ● ● ● ● ● ● ● ●\n💡 the prompt shows which venv is active\n\n./input.yaml\n./.claude/settings.json\n./.claude/.eval-permissions.json\n./hooks/subagent_stop.py\n./cachelib/__init__.py\n./cachelib/SPEC.md\n./cachelib/lru.py\n./tests/.gitkeep\n----\n# LRUCache spec\n\n`LRUCache(capacity: int, ttl: float | None = None, clock=time.monotonic)`\n\n- `get(key, default=None)`: return the value and mark the key as most recently used.\n  Expired entries behave as missing and are removed.\n- `put(key, value)`: insert or update; updating also marks as most recently used.\n  When the cache is over capacity, evict the least recently used entry.\n- `delete(key) -> bool`: remove, return whether it existed.\n- `__len__`, `__contains__` (contains must not change recency, must respect TTL).\n- `stats()` returns `{\"hits\": int, \"misses\": int, \"evictions\": int, \"expirations\": int}`.\n  Expired entries count as a miss and an expiration, not an eviction.\n- `capacity <= 0` raises `ValueError`.\n- All operations O(1) average. Use `collections.OrderedDict`.\n- `clock` is injectable for tests; TTL is measured with it.\n----\nimport time\n\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    def __init__(self, capacity, ttl=None, clock=time.monotonic):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n    def get(self, key, default=None):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n    def put(self, key, value):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n    def delete(self, key):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n    def stats(self):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n    def __contains__(self, key):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n----","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c62ae6b-fdd8-4dfc-ba81-3ddb3b8a69a8","uuid":"0c134a95-7f55-48b2-b239-8edc8aa7e0fb","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:24:21.070Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"                                          alustosa@alustosa-thinkpadp1gen7\n               .',;::::;,'.               ────────────────────────────────\n           .';:cccccccccccc:;,.             OS  Fedora Linux 44 (Workstation Edition) x86_64\n        .;cccccccccccccccccccccc;.          Kernel  Linux 7.1.8-200.fc44.x86_64\n      .:cccccccccccccccccccccccccc:.       󰅐 Uptime  8 days, 19 hours, 51 mins\n    .;ccccccccccccc;.:dddl:.;ccccccc;.      Shell  bash 5.3.9\n   .:ccccccccccccc;OWMKOOXMWd;ccccccc:.     Terminal  claude\n  .:ccccccccccccc;KMMc;cc;xMMc;ccccccc:.  ────────────────────────────────\n  ,cccccccccccccc;MMM.;cc;;WW:;cccccccc,   󰻠 CPU  Intel(R) Core(TM) Ultra 7 165H (12+8+2) @ 5.00 GHz\n  :cccccccccccccc;MMM.;cccccccccccccccc:   󰍛 GPU  Intel Arc Graphics @ 2.30 GHz [Integrated]\n  :ccccccc;oxOOOo;MMM000k.;cccccccccccc:    RAM  50.73 GiB / 62.23 GiB (82%)\n  cccccc;0MMKxdd:;MMMkddc.;cccccccccccc;   󰋊 Disk  247.24 GiB / 952.27 GiB (26%) - btrfs\n  ccccc;XMO';cccc;MMM.;cccccccccccccccc'  ────────────────────────────────\n  ccccc;MMo;ccccc;MMW.;ccccccccccccccc;    󰍹 Display  1920x1200 in 16\", 60 Hz [Built-in]\n  ccccc;0MNc.ccc.xMMd;ccccccccccccccc;     󰍹 Display  1920x1080 in 24\", 144 Hz [External]\n  cccccc;dNMWXXXWM0:;cccccccccccccc:,      󰍹 Display  3440x1440 in 34\", 100 Hz [External]\n  cccccccc;.:odl:.;cccccccccccccc:,.        DE  KDE Plasma 6.7.4\n  ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc:'.          WM  KWin\n  :ccccccccccccccccccccccc:;,..           \n   ':cccccccccccccccc::;,.                  ● ● ● ● ● ● ● ●\n💡 the prompt shows which venv is active\n\n./input.yaml\n./.claude/settings.json\n./.claude/.eval-permissions.json\n./hooks/subagent_stop.py\n./cachelib/__init__.py\n./cachelib/SPEC.md\n./cachelib/lru.py\n./tests/.gitkeep\n----\n# LRUCache spec\n\n`LRUCache(capacity: int, ttl: float | None = None, clock=time.monotonic)`\n\n- `get(key, default=None)`: return the value and mark the key as most recently used.\n  Expired entries behave as missing and are removed.\n- `put(key, value)`: insert or update; updating also marks as most recently used.\n  When the cache is over capacity, evict the least recently used entry.\n- `delete(key) -> bool`: remove, return whether it existed.\n- `__len__`, `__contains__` (contains must not change recency, must respect TTL).\n- `stats()` returns `{\"hits\": int, \"misses\": int, \"evictions\": int, \"expirations\": int}`.\n  Expired entries count as a miss and an expiration, not an eviction.\n- `capacity <= 0` raises `ValueError`.\n- All operations O(1) average. Use `collections.OrderedDict`.\n- `clock` is injectable for tests; TTL is measured with it.\n----\nimport time\n\n\nclass LRUCache:\n    def __init__(self, capacity, ttl=None, clock=time.monotonic):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n    def get(self, key, default=None):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n    def put(self, key, value):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n    def delete(self, key):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n    def stats(self):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n\n    def __contains__(self, key):\n        raise NotImplementedError\n----","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011QRW8aejNXjUqQvvPWd7d4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
