{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CfryTAwqvnqh7DNhfuSQq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Implemented `cachelib/lru.py` per the spec and added `tests/test_lru.py`. All 23 tests pass (`python3 -m pytest tests -q`, run from the case directory). I didn't commit anything.\n\n**Implementation** (`cachelib/lru.py`)\n- Backed by `OrderedDict`, storing `key -> (value, expires_at)`. `get`, `put`, `delete`, and `in` are O(1) average.\n- `capacity <= 0` raises `ValueError`. The clock is injectable and TTL is measured with it.\n- `stats()` returns a fresh dict, so callers can't mutate the counters.\n\n**Choices the spec didn't settle** (easy to change if you want them different):\n- **Expiry boundary:** an entry expires when `now >= set_time + ttl`, so it is already expired at exactly `ttl` seconds.\n- **`__len__`:** counts expired entries that haven't been touched yet. Purging them would make `len` O(n), which conflicts with the O(1) requirement. If you want `len` to exclude expired entries, that's a real change to the design.\n- **`in` and `delete` on expired entries:** `in` and `delete` remove the expired entry and count it as an expiration. Neither counts a hit or miss.\n- **Expired entry pushed out by an insert:** if the LRU entry being evicted is already expired, it counts as an expiration, not an eviction, which follows the spec's rule that expirations are not evictions.\n- **`put` on an existing key:** overwrites the value and resets the TTL. It doesn't count as a hit or miss.\n\n**Tests** (`tests/test_lru.py`) cover basic get/put, LRU ordering (including recency refresh by `get` and by updating `put`), `delete` return values, `in` not changing recency, falsy values as hits, stats counting, TTL expiry through a fake clock, TTL refresh on `put`, expired-entry accounting, capacity 1, and a 1000-operation capacity bound.\n\nI ran the tests with `python3 -m pytest` from the case directory, so `cachelib` is on the import path. I didn't check whether bare `pytest` works."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4515,"cache_read_input_tokens":36482,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4515},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c62ae6b-fdd8-4dfc-ba81-3ddb3b8a69a8","uuid":"966f1e5c-d2c2-4997-b47f-5a8835b534a9","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:24:53.846Z","request_id":"req_011CfryTAdjvAqTUrDPpVNWW"}
